stakeholders = head('Who approves and who benefits', 'The Phoenix board has four equal seats. Three YES votes approve an action. Some payment recipients also took part in approving those payments.') + f'''<div class="wrap page-content">
<section class="reading" id="board-after-4853"><h2>What a removal would leave behind</h2><p>If Vini were removed, the ERIS/Creda and Superbolt relationships would remain among the other directors. Vini is a recorded dissenting voice, but Rose also opposed Estima and voted NO on A272. At an unchanged 75% threshold, three equal remaining seats would still need all three YES votes. A reduction to 60% would let any two approve.</p><a href="/voting/#remaining-board">4853’s possible effects and the safeguards needed</a></section><section id="board"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Phoenix board: four equal seats</h2><p>Each seat has 25 weight; 75% approval means three YES votes. The preserved history contains A1–A289.</p></div>{table(['Director', 'Preserved A1–A289 record', 'Board wallet'], [[r[0], r[1], f'<code>{r[2]}</code>'] for r in director_rows])}<div class="context-note"><strong>0xphilipp’s roles.</strong> The established public handle/address links place 0xphilipp in a Phoenix board seat, the Think Tank technical proposal role, the 50-of-90 ERIS multisig seat, the 4853 proposer/YES-voter role, an ERIS validator role and Treasury beneficiary/OTC relationships. These roles require consistent disclosure and independent checks; they do not prove one key, command structure or coordinated action.</div><div class="two-col"><article><h3>Directors voting on payments to themselves</h3><ul><li>A209 and A215: 0xphilipp proposed and joined Vini and MB in enabling Creda’s 200,000-USDC first three milestones and 10,000-USDC analytics milestone.</li><li>A159: 0xphilipp, Vini and Rose approved an action containing their own recurring compensation.</li><li>A249: Vini proposed and joined the minimum YES set for a 16,900-USDC audit payment to Vini’s address; Rose and MB also approved.</li><li>A271: 0xphilipp, MB and Rose enabled Estima’s first 45,000-USDC payment; Vini was absent.</li></ul></article><article><h3>Proposals directors opposed</h3><ul><li>Rose supplied the only NO on A272; with Vini absent, it failed.</li><li>Vini and Rose rejected the earlier Estima A258; a reduced A266 later passed.</li><li>0xphilipp and Rose rejected A288. MB’s only preserved NO was on the technically corrected A28.</li></ul></article></div>{source_list([('/record/audit/phoenix_board_votes_all.csv', 'Download the complete four-director voting matrix'), ('/record/audit/phoenix/director_vote_patterns.csv', 'Download pairwise and per-director vote patterns'), ('/record/audit/phoenix/key_proposals.json', 'Download key proposal responses')])}</section>
<section id="think-tank"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Think Tank: six voters, effectively 4-of-6</h2><p>A separate veto body—not merely an advisory group. Revoting is disabled and execution is members-only.</p></div>{table(['Member', 'Wallet', 'P1–P5 participation', 'Relevant disclosed/evidenced relationship'], think_rows)}<p>Across four substantive veto proposals, the five non-technical members supplied only two ballots out of 20 possible ballots, both abstentions. P5 contains no executable message; even four YES votes would not itself execute a Treasury veto.</p><p class="note">The technical member abstained on all five proposals. The records do not explain the other missing ballots, and membership has not been checked at every proposal’s block height.</p>{source_list([('/record/audit/thinktank/votes.csv', 'Download all Think Tank ballots'), ('/record/audit/thinktank/proposals.json', 'Download all five proposals'), ('/record/audit/thinktank/members.json', 'Download current membership')])}</section>
<section id="eris-signers"><div class="section-heading"><h2>ERIS fixed multisig: five voters, 90 total weight</h2><p>The absolute threshold is 70. All recorded ballots in P1–P9 are YES; absences therefore matter when assessing how proposals passed or failed.</p></div>{table(['Attribution used', 'Wallet', 'Weight', 'P1–P9 ballots'], eris_rows)}<p>Proposal 9 passed with exactly 70 weight: the 50-weight signer plus two 10-weight signers. Lion DAO’s account executed it after passage; CW3 execution can be permissionless, so execution alone does not prove membership or coordination.</p>{source_list([('/record/audit/eris_multisig_votes_all.csv', 'Download all ERIS multisig ballots'), ('/record/audit/eris_multisig/proposals.json', 'Download all nine proposals'), ('/record/audit/eris_multisig/transactions.json', 'Download preserved multisig transactions')])}</section>
<section id="validators"><div class="section-heading"><h2>Validators, contracts and large holders</h2></div><div class="two-col"><article><h3>Validator ballots differed</h3><p>Galactic Punks, ERIS and Orbital Command voted YES. Smart Stake and Ceres voted VETO. HighStakes voted ABSTAIN. Eleven reviewed allocation-linked validators had no current ballot.</p><p>Only BackBone Labs and cosmosrescue among those unvoted validators had material current hub delegations.</p></article><article><h3>The large vAMP account is unidentified</h3><p>The 215,228-vAMP account remains unattributed. It holds Galactic Punks NFTs and received several direct Galactic Punks transfers, but their reward or payment classification is unresolved.</p><p>NFT holdings, transfers, timing and protocol usage do not establish common ownership.</p></article></div><h3>Other paid contributors and counterparties</h3><p>Recurring core, comms, ambassador and moderator recipients; grant recipients; OTC counterparties; operations contracts; and the ERIS protocol fee account also need payment and approval records. Contract and module accounts must not be mislabeled as people.</p><a href="/treasury/">Continue to treasury and counterparty analysis {ARROW}</a></section>{nextlinks(('/voting/', 'Back: 4853 and voting'), ('/treasury/', 'Next: treasury controls ' + ARROW))}</div>'''
lock_facts = supplement['phoenix_A43_locks']['facts']
